iguration could freeze tool calls; matcher misconfiguration could cause false triggers or missed signals; no existing performance budget documented for PostToolUse hooks.\\n\\n- CI workflows that test hooks \u2014 verify whether `.github/workflows/` or similar includes hook validation. If advisor-trigger is added without CI test coverage, regression risk is high. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Hook behavior is subtle (state management, timing); CI validation is essential; no hook-specific CI tests observed so far.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 Primary consumer of advisor signals. Must document: signal detection (read `advisor_signals` from active-task context), signal interpretation (PLAN = reconsider, CORRECTION = undo, STOP = escalate), worker autonomy (signals are advisory; worker decides whether to comply), logging disagreement as a concern. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Task-worker must correctly interpret advisor verdicts; stale instructions will cause worker to ignore or misinterpret signals, defeating the purpose of the advisor.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` \u2014 May reference advisor in lifecycle or testing context. If grooming produces backlog items that later trigger advisor signals, groomer should be aware of the pattern. | Risk: LOW | Why: Reference-only; no change required unless backlog item structure changes.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/generic-stage-agent.md` \u2014 Base agent pattern. If other agents inherit from this pattern and may encounter advisor signals, document signal handling there. | Risk: LOW | Why: Generic agent is a fallback; most specialized agents will get signals through task-worker context.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/advisor-trigger.cjs` | Role: producer (detects triggers, spawns advisor) | Connection: new hook fires on PostToolUse events, reads active-task context, invokes advisor agent | 