ts exist; advisor-trigger introduces concurrent writes to shared active-task context file; failure mode is silent context corruption\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 `advisor_signals` field contract unverified; schema may not support the field name/type\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 Agent instructions must document signal handling; stale instructions defeat the advisor\\n\\n- **Main risk themes:**\\n  - Invocation bridge undefined (blocker #1 in item): hook cannot call LLM agent directly; subprocess, HTTP sidecar, or queue mechanism must be chosen and implemented\\n  - Async execution required but unspecified (blocker #2): PostToolUse hook that blocks on LLM inference will freeze all tool calls; non-blocking invocation mechanism must be chosen\\n  - Schema contract gaps (blocker #3): `sam_active_task(action='update')` signature must permit `advisor_signals` field; currently assumed but not verified\\n  - Test coverage gap: concurrent PostToolUse hook execution untested; silent context file corruption possible\\n  - Documentation lag: agent inventory, architecture diagram, active-task context schema, task-worker signal handling all require updates\\n\\n- **Scope expansion:**\\n  - Discovered 9 existing hooks in `plugins/development-harness/hooks/` directory \u2014 advisor-trigger follows same pattern\\n  - Discovered active-task context file is shared resource between task_status_hook.py and advisor-trigger.cjs \u2014 concurrent write safety critical\\n  - Discovered no existing test suite for PostToolUse hook concurrency \u2014 first hook to require concurrent execution testing\\n  - Discovered UpdateActiveTaskConfig in sam_schema/core/action_models.py \u2014 advisor_signals field availability unverified; this is critical path blocker\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Hook invocation bridge mechanism decided and implemented (blocker #1 resolved)\\n- [ ] Async/non-blocking invocation mechanism chosen and validated to meet 50ms latency budget (blocker #2 resolved)\\n- [ ] `sam_active_task(action='update', set_fields_json={'advisor_signals': [...]})` verified against actual UpdateActiveTaskConfig schema (blocker #3 resolved)\\n- [ ] Trigger threshold configuration storage decided (config file vs inline defaults; blocker #4 resolution)\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/agents/advisor.md` created with complete prompt\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/hooks/advisor-trigger.cjs` created with event buffer, trigger detection, hook invocation\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` updated with PostToolUse entry\\n- [ ] Concurrent PostToolUse hook tests added to `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/`\\n- [ ] Event buffer tests added (2-failures-in-10-events, 5-Read/Grep-without-Edit detection)\\n- [ ] Timeout and latency tests added (50ms non-triggering path, advisor invocation timeout)\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` updated: add `@dh:advisor` entry to Agents Overview\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` updated: add advisor trigger flow and signal append path\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` updated: document `advisor_signals` field schema and worker consumption\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` updated: document signal detection, interpretation, autonomy model, concern logging\\n- [ ] High-risk path pattern configuration mechanism created (configurable, not hardcoded, per AC requirement)\\n- [ ] CI validation added for hooks (verify hooks.json syntax, test execution)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-09T08:29:39Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-05-09T08:31:39Z \u2014 Replacing with updated priority entry that includes Effort field</summary>\\n\\nScore: 7/10\\nRationale: Addresses active worker loops and destructive-action risk at execution time. Complements #929 (circuit breaker) at the semantic level. Blocked on 4 architectural decisions.\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 one CJS hook file (event buffer, 3 trigger conditions, async invocation) + one agent .md file. Primary uncertainty is the invocation bridge mechanism.\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-09T08:31:39Z</sub>\\n\\nScore: 7/10\\nRationale: Addresses active worker loops and destructive-action risk at execution time. Complements #929 (circuit breaker) at the semantic level. Blocked on 4 architectural decisions.\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 one CJS hook file (event buffer, 3 trigger conditions, async invocation) + one agent .md file. Primary uncertainty is the invocation bridge mechanism.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Alignment assessment: ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Mission alignment\\n\\nItem #2183 proposes a weak-supervision advisor agent that observes agent execution and emits PLAN/CORRECTION/STOP signals based on semantic triggers (repeated failure, plateau detection, high-risk operations). This directly serves the development-harness mission of providing a structured pipeline harness with ARL-derived human touchpoints.\\n\\nCitation: CLAUDE.md (development-harness plugin) \u2014 plugin purpose lines 1-3, ARL human touchpoint model lines 40-41.\\n\\n### Architecture alignment\\n\\nThe proposed PostToolUse hook + agent design fits the existing hook architecture in hooks.json. The current system already uses this pattern:\\n- PostToolUse[Write|Edit|Bash]: task_status_hook.py \u2014 updates task metadata on every tool execution (hooks.json lines 58-68)\\n- PreToolUse[Bash]: block-context-direct-writes.cjs \u2014 pattern-based blocking hook\\n\\nThe advisor follows the same hook lifecycle: event fires \u2192 hook reads context \u2192 hook takes action. The unresolved invocation bridge is an implementation question, not a design misalignment.\\n\\nCitation: plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (accessed 2026-05-09)\\n\\n### Pattern alignment\\n\\nThe advisor's event-buffering requirement (track last 10 tool events per task) follows the registry-file pattern established in stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs (per-session isolation, JSON registry at ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/...). The advisor_signals write via sam_active_task(action='update') follows the active-task context update pattern in task_status_hook.py.\\n\\nCitation: plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs; plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py\\n\\n### Conflicts or duplications\\n\\nIssue #929 (Circuit breaker hook for agent failure loops) addresses raw failure counts via a tool-level reflex. The advisor complements #929 by operating at the semantic level \u2014 repeated same-target failures, plateau patterns, and high-risk path detection. These are different granularities; no duplication.\\n\\nNo existing feature performs semantic signal detection or emits structured advisory verdicts to the active-task context.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-09T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a new feature addition. No existing failure to reproduce.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-09T08:31:23Z</sub>\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a new feature addition. No existing failure to reproduce.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **advisor (weak-supervision) agent emitting plan/correction/stop signals on plateau or repeated failure** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md \u2014 pattern: Advisor (Weak-Supervision Layer) consultative agent triggered on high-risk tasks, repeated failures, or plateau detection; reports PLAN/CORRECTION/STOP signals to executor\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-08)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | PostToolUse hook + advisor agent; three trigger conditions; three-signal schema |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Target files named (`agents/advisor.md`, `hooks/advisor-trigger.cjs`); trigger thresholds enumerated |\\n| External interfaces | DERIVABLE | `sam_active_task(action='update')` is an existing MCP tool used by `task_status_hook.py`; hook invocation pattern established in `hooks.json` |\\n| Constraints (performance) | MISSING | Advisor agent invocation timeout not specified; async vs sync hook execution not stated |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `hooks.json`, CJS hook scripts, `agents/` directory, `task_status_hook.py` all readable |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable signal is concrete \u2014 inspect `active-task-{session}.json` for `advisor_signals` array |\\n\\n**Gaps requiring resolution before execution:**\\n1. How does the hook spawn the advisor agent? Hooks are CJS scripts \u2014 they cannot call MCP tools directly. The invocation bridge (subprocess `claude -p`, HTTP call to a sidecar, or deferred queue) must be decided before implementation.\\n2. Timeout and performance budget for advisor invocation \u2014 a PostToolUse hook that blocks on an LLM call will freeze every tool call. Non-blocking/async invocation is required but the mechanism is unspecified.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Addresses active worker loops and destructive-action risk at execution time. Complements #929 (circuit breaker) by operating at the semantic level. The missing execution-time supervisor is a gap in the current harness pipeline. Blocked items that trigger advisor intervention can save significant wasted agent turns and API cost. However, advisor is consultative (worker may ignore it), so the immediate safety impact is lower than a hard-blocking gate.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 advisor is consultative and does not gate task completion\\n- Bottleneck: Agent loops (same Edit failing repeatedly) currently go unchecked until manual intervention or budget exhaustion\\n- Risk surface: Workers operating on high-risk paths (`**/auth/**`, `**/billing/**`, `*.lock`) have no real-time oversight beyond the planning-time plan-validator\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Reduces wasted turns when a worker is stuck in a repeated-failure or plateau loop\\n- Provides a structured escalation path (STOP \u2192 human) before a worker causes irreversible changes\\n- Complements #929 (raw failure count) with semantic judgment (same fix attempted, wrong approach, high-risk path)\\n- Advisor signals are appended to the active-task context file \u2014 auditable trail of where and why redirection was attempted\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a worker agent triggers one of three conditions \u2014 repeated failure (same tool+target failed twice in 10 events), plateau (5 consecutive Read/Grep with no Edit/Write in 5 minutes), or high-risk path write (target matches configurable pattern) \u2014 the PostToolUse hook fires the advisor. The advisor reads the active-task context and returns one of three signals:\\n\\n- `PLAN` \u2014 worker should reconsider strategy; includes `suggested_approach`\\n- `CORRECTION` \u2014 last action needs immediate undo; includes `required_fix`\\n- `STOP` \u2014 block further automated work; escalate to human\\n\\nThe signal is appended to the active-task context file as an `advisor_signals` array entry. The worker reads it on its next turn. The advisor never owns the final verdict \u2014 the worker decides whether to comply, and disagreement is logged as a concern.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable end state:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/advisor.md` exists and is listed by `git ls-files plugins/development-harness/agents/`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/advisor-trigger.cjs` exists and is referenced in `hooks.json` under `PostToolUse`\\n- When triggered, `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-{session}.json` contains `advisor_signals: [{signal: \\\"CORRECTION\\\"|\\\"PLAN\\\"|\\\"STOP\\\", ts: ..., reason: ...}]`\\n- The hook does not block the triggering tool call \u2014 it fires after tool use completes (non-blocking)\\n- Trigger thresholds are configurable (not hardcoded) so projects can tune without forking the hook\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `git ls-files plugins/development-harness/agents/advisor.md` exits 0\\n2. `hooks.json` lists `advisor-trigger.cjs` under a `PostToolUse` matcher; `jq '.hooks.PostToolUse[] | select(.hooks[].command | contains(\\\"advisor-trigger\\\"))' hooks.json` returns a non-empty result\\n3. Run a task that causes the same Edit to fail twice targeting the same file. Inspect the active-task context JSON \u2014 `advisor_signals` array contains at least one entry with `signal: \\\"CORRECTION\\\"`\\n4. Plateau detection: run a session issuing 5+ consecutive Read/Grep calls without Edit/Write. Advisor fires with `signal: \\\"PLAN\\\"` visible in the context file\\n5. High-risk path: attempt a Write to a path matching `**/auth/**`. Advisor fires with `signal: \\\"STOP\\\"` or `signal: \\\"PLAN\\\"` visible in context\\n6. Hook does not increase per-tool-call latency by more than 50ms in the non-triggering path (advisor invocation is async or skipped entirely when no trigger fires)\\n7. Advisor verdict is non-binding \u2014 worker logs disagreement as a concern but is not blocked from proceeding\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Which invocation bridge should `advisor-trigger.cjs` use to call the advisor agent? Options: (a) `claude -p` subprocess with `--output-format json` (simplest, but adds latency); (b) write a trigger file and use a background daemon; (c) another mechanism.\\n- Should the advisor hook block tool execution when a STOP signal is warranted, or is it always non-blocking (advisory only)? The item says non-binding, but STOP implies urgency.\\n- What is the acceptable latency budget for the hook in the triggering path? (i.e., how long can the advisor LLM call take before it becomes disruptive?)\\n- Should trigger thresholds (2 failures in 10 events, 5 Read/Grep without Edit/Write) be stored in a config file under `.dh/` or embedded as defaults in the hook script?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work \u2014 hook pattern | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/block-context-direct-writes.cjs` |\\n| Prior work \u2014 hook pattern | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs` |\\n| Prior work \u2014 PostToolUse hook | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` (line 58) |\\n| Prior work \u2014 context update pattern | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` |\\n| Research \u2014 advisor pattern | `/home/user/claude_skills/research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md` (Advisor section, lines 80\u201381) |\\n| Research \u2014 improvement proposal | `/home/user/claude_skills/research/insights/2026-05-07-claude-code-harness-improvements.md` (Improvement 4, lines 78\u201397) |\\n| Related agent \u2014 plan-time validation | `@dh:plan-validator` |\\n| Related agent \u2014 post-task verification | `@dh:contract-verification` |\\n| Related agent \u2014 task executor | `@dh:task-worker` |\\n| Skill \u2014 hook creation patterns | `/plugin-creator:hook-creator` |\\n| Skill \u2014 agent creation | `/plugin-creator:agent-creator` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: #929 (Circuit breaker hook for agent failure loops) \u2014 the two patterns are complementary; understanding #929's event-tracking approach informs the advisor trigger's state storage design\\n- Depends on: Resolved invocation bridge question (see Blockers) \u2014 implementation cannot begin until the hook-to-agent call mechanism is decided\\n- Blocks: None currently identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n1. **Hook invocation bridge undefined** \u2014 `advisor-trigger.cjs` is a CJS hook script; hooks cannot call MCP tools directly and cannot spawn advisor as a `claude -p` subagent without a defined bridging mechanism. Options: (a) spawn `claude -p` subprocess with advisor prompt and `--output-format json`, (b) write trigger record to a sidecar queue file that advisor polls, (c) use an HTTP sidecar process. None is specified in the item \u2014 decision required before implementation.\\n2. **Async invocation required but mechanism unspecified** \u2014 Advisor runs LLM inference; blocking PostToolUse hooks freeze all tool calls. The non-blocking invocation pattern (fire-and-forget subprocess, async queue) must be chosen to meet AC #6.\\n3. **`sam_active_task(action='update')` schema for `advisor_signals` not documented** \u2014 the target JSON field name and schema must be verified against the actual MCP tool signature before implementation.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Two deliverables: one CJS hook script and one agent `.md` file. The hook logic (event buffer, trigger detection, threshold evaluation) is non-trivial but follows established patterns in the existing hooks. The advisor agent prompt is straightforward. The unresolved invocation bridge (see Blockers) is the primary uncertainty \u2014 resolving it could increase scope if a sidecar daemon is required.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe dh plugin has no consultative \\\"advisor\\\" agent that observes a worker's progress and emits structured PLAN/CORRECTION/STOP signals. The closest existing patterns:\\n\\n- `@dh:plan-validator` runs once at planning time, not during execution\\n- `@dh:contract-verification` runs once after a task completes \u2014 too late to redirect the worker\\n- `task-worker.md` has internal retry behavior but no external supervisor\\n- Issue #929 (Circuit breaker hook for agent failure loops) tracks consecutive tool failures and injects guidance text \u2014 this is a tool-level reflex, not a strategic supervisor that reads the agent's plan and judges whether to PLAN (try a different approach), CORRECTION (fix what was just done), or STOP (escalate to human)\\n\\nThe Harness Advisor pattern complements #929: the circuit breaker fires on raw failure counts, the Advisor fires on semantic signals (worker proposed a destructive change, worker is on attempt 3 of the same fix, worker is operating on a high-risk file path matching protected patterns).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new agent `plugins/development-harness/agents/advisor.md` and a hook `plugins/development-harness/hooks/advisor-trigger.cjs` registered as a `PostToolUse` handler. The hook detects three trigger conditions on every tool call:\\n\\n1. **Repeated failure** \u2014 same tool + same target failed 2 times in the last 10 events for the active task\\n2. **Plateau detection** \u2014 worker has issued 5 consecutive Read/Grep calls without an Edit/Write in the last 5 minutes\\n3. **High-risk path** \u2014 write target matches a configurable pattern (e.g., `**/auth/**`, `**/billing/**`, `*.lock`)\\n\\nWhen a trigger fires, the hook spawns the advisor agent with the active-task context. Advisor returns one of three structured verdicts:\\n\\n- `{signal: \\\"PLAN\\\", reason: \\\"...\\\", suggested_approach: \\\"...\\\"}` \u2014 worker should reconsider strategy\\n- `{signal: \\\"CORRECTION\\\", reason: \\\"...\\\", required_fix: \\\"...\\\"}` \u2014 last action needs immediate undo\\n- `{signal: \\\"STOP\\\", reason: \\\"...\\\", escalate_to: \\\"human\\\"}` \u2014 block further automated work; surface to user\\n\\nThe verdict is appended to the active-task context file via `sam_active_task(action='update')` so the worker reads it on its next turn. The advisor never owns the final verdict \u2014 the worker decides whether to comply, and disagreement is logged as a concern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun a task that intentionally fails the same Edit twice, then succeeds on the third attempt. Inspect `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-{session}.json` \u2014 it contains an `advisor_signals: [{signal: \\\"CORRECTION\\\", ts: ..., reason: ...}]` array entry. The advisor agent appears in `git ls-files plugins/development-harness/agents/`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7f36eb272eb190449d760ec4fbc8ef3016853becf54a5fa0e656e1d11fa6ede1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuhmLg\"}"}